course: dictionary
lesson: 13604
title: Words for disbelief
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Incredulity is a noun. It means not being able to believe something, and the great surprise that comes with it. You can feel incredulity inside, or you can show it on your face.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The crowd watched the magician make the elephant vanish, and they stared in incredulity.» The crowd is amazed and cannot believe their eyes, so incredulity means disbelief. Try your meaning in the sentence: "they stared in disbelief" still makes sense.
explain: Authors often show incredulity through the body. «Her eyes were wide and her mouth hung open with incredulity.» Wide eyes and an open mouth tell you the character is shocked and does not trust what she has just heard.
explain: Scientists also use this feeling in a healthy way. Healthy incredulity means checking a strange claim carefully before you believe it. Asking "How do we know that is true?" is a good scientific habit.
fact: Incredulity is a noun, the name of a feeling or a state of mind.
fact: Incredulity means not being able to believe something, and great surprise and disbelief.
fact: You can say: stare in incredulity, look in incredulity, or have a look of incredulity.
fact: «Her eyes were wide and her mouth hung open with incredulity.» The face shows the feeling.
fact: In science, healthy incredulity means checking strange claims carefully before believing them.
exercise: «The crowd watched the magician in incredulity.» What does incredulity mean here? | *Not being able to believe what they see | Anger at the magician | Loud cheering and clapping | Feeling very sleepy and bored
exercise: Which face best shows incredulity? | Smiling and waving at friends | Frowning while reading a long book | Yawning with eyes half closed | *Eyes wide and mouth open, as if saying "that can't be true!"
exercise: Scientists talk about healthy incredulity. What does it mean? | Believing every strange claim at once | *Checking a strange claim carefully before believing it | Ignoring all new ideas | Shouting at people who make claims
test: «Tom stared at the flying cat in incredulity.» Which phrase means nearly the same as in incredulity? | Without any sound | In delight | *In disbelief | In a great hurry
test: Choose the phrase that uses incredulity correctly. | A loud song of incredulity | A sleepy incredulity | A bowl of incredulity | *A look of incredulity
exam: Which sentence best shows incredulity? | *He stared at the talking dog, his jaw dropping. | The bus arrived at the usual time. | She ate her lunch and read a book. | They walked slowly home in the rain.
